+// SSRS2 (0055): a worker task is not run by the thread that posts it, wherever that thread can reach the host's
+// thread pool. It was in two cases: posted from a thread on which no isolate is current (a thread pool thread running
+// one of V8's background tasks or jobs, which posts the next), and posted through an isolate that is being torn down.
+// A task run inside its post runs under whatever lock its poster holds (V8 posts foreground tasks under the
+// WebAssembly engine's, 0050), and a job's worker run inside another worker's post is no second worker. V8's own
+// platform always hands a worker task to another thread; so does this one now, on the host's thread pool, tied to no
+// isolate (a task that belongs to an isolate is cancelable and finds itself canceled once its isolate is gone).
+// The host is called through the method table it gives a thread for the length of a call it makes into this library
+// (V8SplitProxyManaged): a thread of this library's own has none. Such are the threads that run the worker tasks of
+// the snapshot creator's isolate (0027), whose jobs post their next workers from there: on them the task is run in
+// place, as it always was.
+static void Ssrs2RunOnWorkerThread(std::unique_ptr<v8::Task> upTask)
+{
+    if (!V8SplitProxyManaged::Ssrs2CanCallHost())
+    {
+        upTask->Run();
+        return;
+    }
+
+    std::shared_ptr<v8::Task> spTask(std::move(upTask));
+    HostObjectUtil::QueueNativeCallback([spTask] () { spTask->Run(); });
+}
